From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] turnip: kgsl: don't fail instance creation with KHR_display

Vulkan loaders and WSI layers (zink, vkcube, wlroots' Vulkan renderer)
enable VK_KHR_display whenever the instance offers it. The KGSL backend
refused to load at all then ("I can't KHR_display"), so no Vulkan device
showed up. KHR_display is just unusable on KGSL (no DRM master); every
other path works, so carry on without it.
---
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -1898,7 +1898,7 @@
 VkResult
 tu_knl_kgsl_load(struct tu_instance *instance, int fd)
 {
-   if (instance->vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_display) {
+   if (false && instance->vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_display) { /* winglm: KHR_display just unusable on kgsl, not fatal */
       return vk_errorf(instance, VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED,
                        "I can't KHR_display");
    }
